<title>USA: CBOT June volume up 10.4 pct yr/yr to 18.97 mln.</title>
<headline>CBOT June volume up 10.4 pct yr/yr to 18.97 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade (CBOT) said Wednesday trading volume in its futures and options totaled 18,970,531 contracts in June, up 10.4. percent, from 17,181,243 in June 1996.</p>
<p>Volume in major categories and in selected individual contracts is as follows:</p>
<p>			June 1997   % change	June 1996</p>
<p>All futures	15,050,399	+13.5     13,255,063</p>
<p>  Agricultural    4,227,111	+ 6.9	3,955,601</p>
<p>  Financial	10,821,402	+16.4	9,296,087</p>
<p>All options on:</p>
<p>  Futures	   3,920,132	- 0.2	3,926,180</p>
<p>  Agricultural    1,188,254	+ 2.5	1,159,092</p>
<p>  Financial	 2,729,678	- 1.3	2,765,488</p>
<p>Futures (individual):</p>
<p>  US T-bonds	7,400,244	+13.5	6,520,569</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes  1,942,300	+13.2	1,715,630</p>
<p>  US 5-yr notes   1,143,832	+30.2	  878,305</p>
<p>  Wheat		 469,158	- 8.5	  512,883</p>
<p>  Corn		1,347,471	-12.8	1,545,071</p>
<p>  Soybeans	  1,355,599	+37.0	  989,480</p>
<p>  Soymeal	     569,760	+28.8	  442,370</p>
<p>  Soyoil		439,626	+ 3.9	  423,089</p>
<p>Options (individual):</p>
<p>  US T-bonds	2,155,885	+ 6.0	2,033,741</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes    362,507	-30.1	  518,607</p>
<p>  Corn		  376,014	-33.6	  566,551</p>
<p>  Soybeans	    585,753	+69.4	  345,714</p>
<p>((--Chicago derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
